WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.040
AC Fowler: One of these watches

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.850
is a vintage Rolex Submariner,

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.570
estimated to be worth up to $30,000.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.543
The other? A total knockoff.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.276
With replicas steadily improving

00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:12.810
in quality and detail,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.790
it can be difficult to
tell the difference.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.790
So we headed to luxury consignment shop

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.148
The RealReal to meet with

00:00:18.148 --> 00:00:19.750
one of its authenticity experts

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.102
and learn some tips on how

00:00:21.102 --> 00:00:23.390
the average shopper can spot a knockoff.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.608
Laif Anderson: Remember your training.

00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:25.810
[laughing]

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.718
AC: Laif has gathered

00:00:26.718 --> 00:00:28.577
five pairs of luxury watches.

00:00:28.577 --> 00:00:30.918
One is real, and one is a replica,

00:00:30.918 --> 00:00:32.468
and I'm gonna see how well I do

00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:33.810
telling them apart.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.500
So, by the end, I'll be able to hopefully

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.580
have some tips to authenticate like a pro.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.790
How do you think I'm gonna do?

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.109
Laif: I think you're gonna test how good

00:00:40.109 --> 00:00:42.327
your eyes are and your
attention to details,

00:00:42.327 --> 00:00:43.693
but I think you're gonna come out on top.

00:00:43.693 --> 00:00:44.526
AC: All right, let's go.

00:00:44.526 --> 00:00:45.367
Laif: All right.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.080
The first thing we're gonna do is

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.780
we're gonna kit you out
to handle the watches.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.890
AC: OK, what does that mean?

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.590
Laif: That means that we have

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.270
certain precautions that we use

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.693
to handle the watches so that we don't

00:00:58.693 --> 00:01:00.090
leave any kind of
fingerprints or anything,

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.880
especially if we have to open the watches

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.350
to authenticate or just
handle them in general.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.780
So, the first thing we're gonna do

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.180
is we're gonna put on what are called

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.129
finger cots.

00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:14.957
AC: All right, here we go.

00:01:14.957 --> 00:01:15.790
Laif: There you go.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.460
And the next thing you're
gonna need is a loupe.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.293
AC: OK, a loupe.

00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:19.630
Laif: I've already got mine on,

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.530
but you're gonna need it.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.760
This helps support
magnification over one eye

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.680
while you're manipulating
things with both hands.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.130
AC: OK.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.310
I have no idea how to
start even with this.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.897
Laif: So, I think that's
a good way to start it,

00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:32.005
just this wire is a little bit loose,

00:01:32.005 --> 00:01:33.710
so you can cross over like that.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.217
AC: OK, very cool. Wow.

00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:36.095
Laif: And make sure you got a

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.120
pretty good field of vision,

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.644
you can just pop that up on your forehead

00:01:38.644 --> 00:01:39.720
after you feel comfortable.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.630
AC: OK, cool.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.640
I mean, just with this,
I feel more confident.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.880
Laif: We're gonna dive right in.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.860
I'm gonna show you two watches.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.601
These are two Hublot Big Bangs.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.790
They're a Swiss Company,
much like the majority

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.601
of the watches that we
sell on The RealReal.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:54.173
They're a very storied company.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.240
The key elements, things
that we're gonna look for,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.710
are in the fit and finish.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:01.543
AC: OK.

00:02:01.543 --> 00:02:03.180
The fit. And the fish.
Laif: And finish.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.740
Especially in these watches where they use

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.300
so many unique components.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.780
So, you wanna look at
the printing on the dial,

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.820
you wanna look at the
numbers, also on the bezel,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.090
they have these bezel screws,

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.470
you wanna look at the
fit and finish of those.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.553
How crisp and clean everything is.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.127
AC: All right, it says Hublot Big Bang,

00:02:21.127 --> 00:02:22.130
so I feel like that's a good sign

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:22.963
for this one?

00:02:22.963 --> 00:02:24.350
Laif: Mm-hmm.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.490
AC: It says titanium, but
it might just say that,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.340
maybe it's not actually titanium.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.562
I'm gonna feel the weight to see

00:02:30.562 --> 00:02:33.043
if it feels like titanium.

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:36.463
I guess I have no idea.

00:02:36.463 --> 00:02:37.890
[laughing]

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:38.723
All right, cool.

00:02:38.723 --> 00:02:40.330
So, but I also need to put it on, right?

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.100
You said the wear is a big part of it too.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.070
OK, cool.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.010
It fits me perfectly.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.360
I'm made for this lifestyle.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.410
I think that's one of
my biggest takeaways.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:49.638
It also upside down. [laughs]

00:02:49.638 --> 00:02:52.140
Laif: I was gonna let you figure that out.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.440
AC: All right. Yes, great.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.470
All right, I feel like I know some things

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.303
about this watch.

00:02:58.303 --> 00:02:59.574
Laif: OK.
AC: But I'm gonna inspect

00:02:59.574 --> 00:03:01.450
the other one to see if I'm right.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.670
All right, switch.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.410
Laif: OK, switching.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.243
AC: All right, automatically,

00:03:05.243 --> 00:03:06.760
I feel like this one's
a little bit heavier.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:07.593
Laif: It's a little bit larger,

00:03:07.593 --> 00:03:08.720
so that's not to be unexpected.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:09.553
AC: Yeah, right.

00:03:09.553 --> 00:03:12.298
I can already tell that
the screws on this one

00:03:12.298 --> 00:03:14.400
are a little bit cleaner.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.850
So, yeah, that might mean something,

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:17.875
or it might not.

00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:19.860
[laughing]

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.643
The numbers are pretty
similar on this one too.

00:03:24.296 --> 00:03:25.550
I feel like I learned nothing from that,

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.983
so I'm just gonna put it
on and see how it feels.

00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:31.149
OK, I really like how this one feels.

00:03:31.149 --> 00:03:32.588
I think I know which one is real

00:03:32.588 --> 00:03:33.696
and which one is fake.

00:03:33.696 --> 00:03:35.921
So, after examining both Hublots,

00:03:35.921 --> 00:03:38.554
I think the real one is

00:03:38.554 --> 00:03:39.920
this one right here.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.763
With the black rim, a little bit heavier,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.740
slightly nicer screws,

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.330
so I feel like I'm gonna say this one.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.823
Laif: OK. That is your guess.

00:03:49.823 --> 00:03:51.220
[AC laughing]

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.780
AC: OK, and am I right?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.150
Laif: Well, no.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.019
You're wrong.

00:03:56.019 --> 00:03:57.893
It is a super fake, so

00:03:57.893 --> 00:03:59.820
I will give you super credit

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.160
for looking at the details that you did.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.200
AC: Super credit, wow.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.466
Laif: But not being familiar

00:04:03.466 --> 00:04:05.267
with what it should be,

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:06.833
that's where they get you.

00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:08.270
AC: OK, cool.
Laif: Starting off,

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.613
we're gonna look at the dial printing,

00:04:10.613 --> 00:04:12.863
and you can see that
the "Hublot" on this one

00:04:12.863 --> 00:04:15.788
is raised, it's very sheen,

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.927
it has a nice fit and finish to it.

00:04:17.927 --> 00:04:19.735
Also, all of the numbers

00:04:19.735 --> 00:04:21.980
are very tight and clean.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.755
The printing of Hublot on the dial

00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:25.546
is one of the bigger tells,

00:04:25.546 --> 00:04:28.320
because it's not very finished.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.800
It's not raised like this one,

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.380
it was what we would expect to see.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.780
AC: All right. So, I definitely

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.563
failed the first round, but I feel

00:04:34.563 --> 00:04:36.340
like I can do it on this next round.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.173
So what do we have?

00:04:37.173 --> 00:04:38.131
Laif: For round two,

00:04:38.131 --> 00:04:40.230
we have the Omega Seamasters.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.080
We'll take them off the
cuff, because these,

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.856
we want to inspect every angle,

00:04:45.856 --> 00:04:47.010
all the fine details

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.330
as well as the case back,

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.050
'cause these have a special engraving.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.253
This has a hippocampus on the back.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:00.410
AC: It's pretty well
crafted from what I can see.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.435
All right, I'm gonna try it on

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:04.470
to see how it fits.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.250
Feels good. Not too heavy, not too light.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.730
Hand me the next one, sir!

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:09.563
Laif: OK.

00:05:09.563 --> 00:05:11.952
This one is a slightly different model,

00:05:11.952 --> 00:05:13.700
but that's half the fun.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.580
AC: I feel like this is a big deal.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.360
This one, the hippocampus,

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.630
and all the things that
are happening on the back

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.730
are sort of raised.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.510
And they're, like, engraved on the back,

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.990
which I feel like might
be an important sign.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:29.856
All right. So, this is what

00:05:29.856 --> 00:05:30.814
I'm gonna do for this one,

00:05:30.814 --> 00:05:32.103
'cause I didn't do it for the last one:

00:05:32.103 --> 00:05:33.570
I'm gonna look at them both together,

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:34.495
which I feel like

00:05:34.495 --> 00:05:36.237
is really gonna help me see things.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:42.190
I'm gonna make a guess, an educated guess,

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.023
and I'm gonna say

00:05:45.865 --> 00:05:50.310
that this one is the real watch.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.497
Laif: OK.
[AC laughing]

00:05:53.497 --> 00:05:54.790
AC: Am I right?

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.120
Laif: You are not right.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.220
You were fooled again.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.120
One of the things that you didn't do

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.990
was you didn't check the bezel.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.367
This bezel doesn't turn.

00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:04.301
AC: Ah, OK.

00:06:04.301 --> 00:06:06.940
Laif: That one does.
AC: Oh, wow!

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.399
Laif: And all dive watches
that have dive bezels,

00:06:09.399 --> 00:06:12.000
they'll have a unidirectional bezel,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.630
meaning it only turns in one direction.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.050
So that's a pretty big tell.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.937
But, again, you're
dealing with a super fake,

00:06:17.937 --> 00:06:20.370
you did admirable, you know,

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.520
they're very hard to tell apart.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.040
AC: Thanks for trying
to make me feel better.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.773
This is not going well. But I feel,

00:06:25.773 --> 00:06:27.700
I still feel confident
for some reason. [laughs]

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.020
I can still meet the goal I set

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.200
of getting three of these right.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.960
So let's just hop into the next one.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:32.793
What do we have?

00:06:32.793 --> 00:06:35.420
Laif: Next we're gonna look
at Cartier Santos 100s.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.586
AC: Wow, these are beautiful.

00:06:36.586 --> 00:06:38.011
Laif: These are beautiful watches.

00:06:38.011 --> 00:06:39.675
These are one of the best sellers

00:06:39.675 --> 00:06:40.980
that we have at The RealReal.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:42.140
These are meant to be worn.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:42.973
AC: OK.

00:06:42.973 --> 00:06:44.164
Laif: I mean, the artistry is there,

00:06:44.164 --> 00:06:46.372
and Cartier does it probably better

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.720
than anybody else.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.450
Their designs are fabulous,

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.480
but these are functional micromachines.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.440
Have a look at these.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:54.860
AC: All right.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.035
Laif: And, again, we're looking

00:06:56.035 --> 00:06:57.885
at fit and finish.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.120
AC: I'm gonna put this
one on the table for now

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.540
and take a look at this other one here.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:06.440
Laif: OK.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.270
AC: Now, this one, I'm
already seeing some wear,

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.140
which is perhaps a good sign,

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.600
