00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.999
Like, they don't always
go around the diamond,

00:07:53.999 --> 00:07:56.140
it's kind of messy on the side here.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:00.240
So I feel like a real Cartier watch

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.640
would've gotten that right.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.040
So, here we go.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.810
This is a very important round.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.050
Out of these two watches,

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:09.423
I do believe this one is the real watch.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.512
Laif: You got it.
AC: Yes!

00:08:13.512 --> 00:08:14.870
Laif: That is it. That is it.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.169
AC: Excellent. All right, yes!

00:08:16.169 --> 00:08:17.169
So, I got that one right,

00:08:17.169 --> 00:08:18.244
now we're on to the fourth one,

00:08:18.244 --> 00:08:19.840
we're nearing the finish line.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:20.980
What do we have here?

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.938
Laif: OK, so what have here

00:08:22.938 --> 00:08:25.500
are two vintage Rolex Submariners.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.733
These sold for less than $1,000

00:08:27.733 --> 00:08:28.816
