00:09:06.243 --> 00:09:07.853
So, if you do a quick cup test

00:09:07.853 --> 00:09:10.430
of the watch, you just
block out all the light,

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.770
you shouldn't see any glowing.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.290
AC: OK, this one is actually glowing.

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:15.326
And so you don't want

00:09:15.326 --> 00:09:16.488
to see it glowing, is what you're saying?

00:09:16.488 --> 00:09:17.880
Laif: We would not expect to see that.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.063
They stopped using tritium on the dials

00:09:20.063 --> 00:09:21.650
in about 1995.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:22.483
AC: OK.

00:09:22.483 --> 00:09:23.733
Laif: OK, so we're getting a reaction

00:09:23.733 --> 00:09:25.040
from the blacklight here.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.180
AC: OK, cool.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:27.260
Laif: Check this one.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.812
AC: No.
Laif: No reaction.

00:09:28.812 --> 00:09:30.553
AC: OK, cool. I think I know

00:09:30.553 --> 00:09:32.020
which one is the real

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:33.580
and which one is the fake.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:34.710
Or should I say The RealReal?

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.510
I think...nay, I know,

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.929
the real one is

00:09:39.929 --> 00:09:40.970
this one.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:41.961
Laif: You are correct.

00:09:41.961 --> 00:09:44.470
AC: Oh, yes!

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.800
Laif: Redemption is right there!

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:46.633
AC: I will say you gave me

00:09:46.633 --> 00:09:47.550
a lot of hints, so. [laughs]

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.190
Laif: Yeah, I did on this one.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.560
Because you're feeling so confident

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.023
and you're doing so well, we're gonna

00:09:52.023 --> 00:09:53.190
make this a little bit harder for you.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.023
AC: OK.

00:09:54.023 --> 00:09:55.610
Laif: I'm just gonna give you one watch.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.168
I'm not gonna tell you anything about it.

00:09:57.168 --> 00:09:58.001
You're gonna have to use

00:09:58.001 --> 00:09:58.944
everything that you've learned.

00:09:58.944 --> 00:09:59.860
AC: All my skills.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.230
Laif: All your skills.
AC: OK.

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:02.063
Laif: This is it.

00:10:02.063 --> 00:10:03.763
This is the moment that you move

00:10:03.763 --> 00:10:05.104
from student to master.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:06.200
AC: All right.
Laif: This is it.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.690
So, this is a Cartier Pasha.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:09.523
AC: OK.

00:10:09.523 --> 00:10:10.923
And this is more like real life,

00:10:10.923 --> 00:10:14.314
because when someone brings you a watch,

00:10:14.314 --> 00:10:15.280
you don't really have another one,

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.730
necessarily, to look at it next to.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.563
Laif: Exactly.

00:10:17.563 --> 00:10:19.440
This is exactly how we experience it.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.010
AC: OK, all right, here we go.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.270
I'm going in.

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:24.580
Cartier No. 2, watch No. 5.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.807
Laif: Remember your training.

00:10:25.807 --> 00:10:27.430
[laughing]

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.920
AC: Everything seems very sturdy.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.350
I'm gonna open this up.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.590
How do you open this? [laughs]

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.380
Laif: It does, has a mystery clasp,

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.230
and this what they call a butterfly clasp,

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.357
'cause it opens on two sides.

00:10:38.357 --> 00:10:39.257
AC: Oh, no way!

00:10:39.257 --> 00:10:40.090
Laif: You use your finger under one side,

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:40.973
and pop.

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:42.100
AC: Oh, wow!

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.760
Laif: So it pops up on both sides.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.360
Opens like a butterfly's wings.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.734
AC: That is a pretty cool design element.

00:10:47.734 --> 00:10:49.300
[sighs]

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:50.860
After careful consideration,

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:53.443
I do believe that this watch

00:10:53.443 --> 00:10:55.384
is, in fact, real.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:58.330
Laif: Are you sure?

00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.988
AC: And by real, I do mean fake.

00:10:59.988 --> 00:11:01.338
[laughing]

00:11:01.338 --> 00:11:02.560
No, I said real, it's fine.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:03.393
Oh, gosh!

00:11:03.393 --> 00:11:05.734
Laif: Yeah, yeah, this is a tough one.

00:11:05.734 --> 00:11:07.470
AC: This is why you're the master,

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.870
and this is the reason
why I am not. [laughs]

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.505
Laif: The big tell is
if we flip this over,

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:16.909
the movement is not what we would expect

00:11:16.909 --> 00:11:18.890
to see for the finish.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.273
AC: Wow! Well, thank you so much!

00:11:20.273 --> 00:11:21.106
It was great.

00:11:21.106 --> 00:11:22.437
Laif: It was absolutely my pleasure.

00:11:22.437 --> 00:11:24.760
I'll expect you at 9:30 on Monday.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.610
AC: Right, yes, exactly. [laughs]

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:27.685
Laif: We'll get you working.

00:11:27.685 --> 00:11:29.360
AC: For lesson two. [laughs]

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.200
I'm gonna take these off because

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.508
my fingers are sweating.

